  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Human centered approach and decent work agenda reflected in the United Nations Sustainable Development Cooperation Framework</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ILO&#x2019;s communication efforts in Lebanon aim to address the critical challenge of promoting decent work principles while fostering greater awareness of and engagement with the ILO&#x2019;s work in Lebanon, in alignment with the ILO Regional Communication Strategy. They focus on partnerships, capacity building and targeted advocacy to advance the ILO&#x2019;s mission of promoting decent work, address social inequalities and foster stronger multi-stakeholder collaboration to achieve broader socio-economic goals in Lebanon.
The expected results include increased visibility and understanding of ILO initiatives, enhanced collaboration among stakeholders and strengthened policy coherence to advance sustainable development. These efforts are designed to amplify the impact of ILO&#x2019;s programmes and ensure alignment with national priorities and the broader UN Development Cooperation Framework for 2024&#x2013;2025. 
The primary beneficiaries of these communication efforts are ILO constituents, development partners, UN agencies, other relevant institutions and the general public. Communication work is implemented with strategic partners such as UN agencies, international and local organizations, media outlets and civil society institutions.</narrative>
  </description>
